<article class="env-lemma" id="056Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/056Z">Lemma <span data-tag="056Z">37.23.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $x \in X$ be a point with image $s \in S$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is flat at $x$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{O}_{X_ s, x}$ has $\text{depth} \geq 1$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists an affine open neighbourhood $U \subset X$ of $x$ and an effective Cartier divisor $D \subset U$ containing $x$ such that $D \to S$ is flat and of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Pick any $h \in \mathfrak m_ x \subset \mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ which maps to a nonzerodivisor in $\mathcal{O}_{X_ s, x}$ and apply Lemma <a href="/tag/056Y" data-tag="056Y">37.23.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>